            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Centralized Identity</h2>
                    <p>Diagrams and short text showing clients obtaining tokens from an identity provider and forwarding them to services.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-text">Client → Identity Server → JWT Token → API Gateway → Services

All services validate tokens from the same identity provider</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>JWT Validation in Services</h2>
                    <p>Program.cs example showing JWT Bearer authentication setup and a sample authorization policy for scopes/claims.</p>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Program.cs
builder.Services.AddAuthentication(JwtBearerDefaults.AuthenticationScheme)
    .AddJwtBearer(options =&gt;
    {
        options.Authority = "https://identity-server";
        options.Audience = "orders-api";
        options.TokenValidationParameters = new TokenValidationParameters
        {
            ValidateIssuer = true,
            ValidateAudience = true,
            ValidateLifetime = true
        };
    });

builder.Services.AddAuthorization(options =&gt;
{
    options.AddPolicy("OrdersRead", policy =&gt;
        policy.RequireClaim("scope", "orders.read"));
});

// Controller
[Authorize(Policy = "OrdersRead")]
public async Task&lt;IActionResult&gt; GetOrders() { }</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Service-to-Service Auth</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">// Client Credentials Flow for service-to-service
builder.Services.AddHttpClient&lt;IInventoryClient, InventoryClient&gt;()
    .AddClientCredentialsTokenHandler("inventory-api");</code></pre>
                </section>

                <LessonTakeaways>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Use centralized identity provider (Keycloak, Duende).</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Each service validates JWT tokens.</LessonTakeaway>
                    <LessonTakeaway>Client Credentials for service-to-service.</LessonTakeaway>
                </LessonTakeaways>
            </div>
